  "body": "Part 2 of #917. The maintainer's direction on #917: the app uses solidcore for all STEP reading, and no second STEP path stays.\n\n## What is wrong\n\nAfter part 1 of #917, the STEP importer reads through solidcore. These readers in `crates/app/src/geometry/import/` still use `ruststep`:\n\n- `step_csys.rs` (the tool-body coordinate reader, used by the `tool_body*` commands)\n- `step_units.rs`\n- `step_depth.rs`\n\nThus the app has two STEP parsers.\n\n## What to do\n\n- Port the three readers to the `solidcore-step` p21 parser.\n- Remove `ruststep` from `crates/app/Cargo.toml`.\n- Keep the behaviour: the same results for the `tool_csys_*.step` fixtures, the same refusals, no crash and no hang on corrupt input.\n- Keep the nesting limit of `step_depth.rs`, or show that the new parser has an equal limit.\n\n## Order\n\nThis issue is stacked on the PR of part 1 of #917. Work it after that PR, one PR at a time, with its own gate.\n\nRefs #917\n",
